  "title": "2026-09-08-comp-134600 · sandboxed-tool-fleet",
  "description": "# Sandboxed tool-execution fleet\nRead the four bands top to bottom, with local flows left to right.\n\n1. **Placement service:** the agent supplies an image and resource class. Concurrent-environment and aggregate-runtime quotas gate admission; excess requests wait fairly. A compatible warm instance returns immediately; a miss selects a healthy host with capacity and waits for cold boot before returning a lease.\n2. **Environment lifecycle:** provisioning → ready → leased → idle → draining → destroyed. Fixed-term leases require renewal heartbeats. The reclaimer destroys expired instances rather than returning tenant filesystem or process state to the pool. Every instance has an absolute maximum age. Image releases mark older instances draining, prohibit new leases, and let active work finish before destruction.\n3. **Within a lease:** each call has timeout, memory, CPU, and network limits. All egress uses an allowlisting proxy. Output streams are capped; durable files go to a session-keyed artifact store because local state is ephemeral. Overlong calls are killed and reported as TIMEOUT, not tool errors.\n4. **Fleet operations:** the supervisor observes host capacity, warm-pool depth, and demand to adjust pre-booted supply. Repeated boot failures quarantine hosts and exclude them from placement. Operations monitor boot latency, reclamations, tool timeouts, and escape-attempt signals.\n\nBlue regions describe control-plane admission and supply; teal describes lifecycle enforcement; violet describes leased execution. Red paths emphasize reclamation and failure handling; dashed paths show image retirement.",
